# 0009 accel: zero-copy display flip through the GGTT slots, with the copy path kept as a fallback
#
# Base:  NvGfx xe 5a19a73f36249efb99c44c3f9cb34603ef0c0eb8 (XeGfx 0.0.44)
# Requires: patches/0002-accel-vblank-and-head4.patch
# Files: kexts/NVRM/accel/nvrm-accel.cpp (modified)
#        kexts/NVRM/accel/xegfx_accel_names.h (modified: sysctl-visible names for the new counters)
# Apply: patch -p1 < patches/0009-accel-zero-copy-flip.patch
#
# The copy path costs a 16 MB CPU copy per frame.  With the frame's physical pages known (surface
# IOMemoryDescriptor) and XeGfx's GGTT slots available, the tx path now maps the frame into a free slot,
# writes PLANE_SURF_1_A once (the plane arms it at the next vblank), and keeps the two previous frames
# mapped until a later flip proves they are no longer scanned.  debug.xegfxaccel_iop_xe_flip=0 falls back
# to the copy path at any time.  The counters that made the diagnosis possible are kept: surf_repeat /
# same_refresh / copy_overrun / copy_cross / src_changed and the surface-map timings; the rest is the flip
# state machine and its sysctl registrations.
#
